1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,388
We would like to share our
development strategy and

2
00:00:05,443 --> 00:00:08,340
direction for the new JEI
English program in the U.S.

3
00:00:10,090 --> 00:00:15,010
We aim to develop a new JEI English
program centered on literacy development.

4
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:20,760
What sets the new JEI English program
apart is not simply more literacy content.

5
00:00:21,210 --> 00:00:25,695
While our current program already develops
foundational language and basic literacy

6
00:00:25,749 --> 00:00:30,073
skills, the new program will integrate
literacy instruction, precise assessment,

7
00:00:30,127 --> 00:00:34,720
personalized learning, and progress tracking
into one integrated learning experience.

8
00:00:36,370 --> 00:00:40,210
More specifically, we want students
to go beyond reading English.

9
00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:45,370
We want them to understand texts, make
decisions, and express their own ideas.

10
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:49,535
Through precise assessment,
we will identify each

11
00:00:49,586 --> 00:00:52,460
student's current level and
areas that need improvement.

12
00:00:52,910 --> 00:00:55,369
We will then provide a
personalized learning path and

13
00:00:55,415 --> 00:00:57,920
use learning results to track
each student's progress.

14
00:00:59,570 --> 00:01:03,110
In U.S. education, literacy means
more than reading comprehension.

15
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:05,630
It goes beyond understanding texts.

16
00:01:06,080 --> 00:01:08,997
Literacy also includes
understanding complex texts,

17
00:01:09,054 --> 00:01:12,200
using evidence to make
decisions, and expressing ideas.

18
00:01:13,850 --> 00:01:17,000
These skills also support learning
across different subjects.

19
00:01:17,450 --> 00:01:20,781
For our new program, we plan to
connect basic language skills, such

20
00:01:20,831 --> 00:01:24,460
as Phonics, Vocabulary, and Grammar,
with Reading, Writing, and Thinking.

21
00:01:24,910 --> 00:01:28,025
Our goal is to help students move
beyond reading comprehension

22
00:01:28,076 --> 00:01:30,940
to deeper understanding,
decision-making, and expression.

23
00:01:32,690 --> 00:01:36,233
We also reviewed NCTE's major
education directions over the past

24
00:01:36,288 --> 00:01:39,720
ten years and their possible
direction for the next ten years.

25
00:01:40,170 --> 00:01:43,154
Over the past decade, digital
and media literacy, along

26
00:01:43,209 --> 00:01:46,410
with critical literacy, have
been important areas of focus.

27
00:01:46,860 --> 00:01:50,417
These areas emphasize reading
and evaluating texts critically,

28
00:01:50,474 --> 00:01:53,400
making independent decisions,
and expressing ideas.

29
00:01:55,050 --> 00:01:57,602
Looking ahead, the growing
use of AI agents is

30
00:01:57,657 --> 00:02:00,320
expected to make new skills
even more important.

31
00:02:00,770 --> 00:02:04,453
These include understanding and
using AI critically, human-centered

32
00:02:04,508 --> 00:02:08,300
writing, digital citizenship, and
expressing ideas in different ways.

33
00:02:09,950 --> 00:02:12,514
Based on these findings,
our English team plans

34
00:02:12,569 --> 00:02:15,460
to develop a program that
goes beyond basic literacy.

35
00:02:15,910 --> 00:02:18,158
We want students to evaluate information

36
00:02:18,214 --> 00:02:20,800
and express their ideas
clearly and logically.

37
00:02:22,550 --> 00:02:26,179
According to the 2024 NAEP
results, reading achievement

38
00:02:26,245 --> 00:02:29,280
in the U.S. remains below
pre-pandemic levels.

39
00:02:29,730 --> 00:02:32,411
Only about 30% of Grade
4 and Grade 8 students

40
00:02:32,469 --> 00:02:34,800
reached the Proficient level in reading.

41
00:02:36,450 --> 00:02:39,444
Both grades also showed a five-point drop

42
00:02:39,517 --> 00:02:42,730
in average reading scores
from 2019 to 2024.

43
00:02:43,180 --> 00:02:45,800
These results show a
continued need to improve

44
00:02:45,857 --> 00:02:48,250
reading comprehension and literacy skills.

45
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:54,480
Parents increasingly want personalized
learning and clear evidence of progress.

46
00:02:54,930 --> 00:02:58,338
JEI already has strong assessment
and learning systems, but our

47
00:02:58,392 --> 00:03:01,800
strengths and learning results
are not always clear to parents.

48
00:03:03,450 --> 00:03:07,021
To address this, we plan to use
online Adaptive Assessment to better

49
00:03:07,074 --> 00:03:10,750
identify each student's current level
and areas that need improvement.

50
00:03:11,200 --> 00:03:13,610
We will then provide a
personalized learning

51
00:03:13,665 --> 00:03:16,020
roadmap that parents
can easily understand.

52
00:03:16,470 --> 00:03:20,247
We also plan to improve our reports
so parents can clearly see progress

53
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:24,290
and achievement for each learning
objective, supported by learning results.

54
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:29,260
We also reviewed opportunities
in the U.S. education market.

55
00:03:29,710 --> 00:03:32,416
Although the market is already
well developed, we found

56
00:03:32,465 --> 00:03:35,270
that parents continue to show
demand for extra education.

57
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:37,830
They are also still
willing to spend money on

58
00:03:37,877 --> 00:03:40,080
additional learning support
for their children.

59
00:03:40,530 --> 00:03:45,020
This shows that there are still opportunities
for JEI in the U.S. education market.

60
00:03:46,770 --> 00:03:49,822
We reviewed major competitors
to understand how each brand

61
00:03:49,875 --> 00:03:53,190
is positioned in the market and
what direction JEI should take.

62
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:57,240
Kumon is known for repeated practice
and building learning habits.

63
00:03:57,690 --> 00:04:00,860
Eye Level focuses on level-based
personalized learning.

64
00:04:01,310 --> 00:04:04,470
Best Brains focuses on instruction
by qualified teachers.

65
00:04:04,920 --> 00:04:09,490
Huntington focuses on test preparation
and improving academic results.

66
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:14,227
We believe JEI has limited
opportunities to stand out if

67
00:04:14,282 --> 00:04:17,590
we compete only on repeated
practice, test scores, or price.

68
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:21,660
Instead, we need to build on our
strength in precise assessment.

69
00:04:23,310 --> 00:04:26,313
We want to clearly show what
each student's learning problems

70
00:04:26,362 --> 00:04:29,660
are, what they need to learn next,
and how much they have improved.

71
00:04:30,110 --> 00:04:33,150
In other words, we want to
connect assessment, personalized

72
00:04:33,201 --> 00:04:35,520
learning paths, and clear
evidence of growth.

73
00:04:37,170 --> 00:04:40,140
Our goal is to build a clear
position around the message:

74
00:04:40,690 --> 00:04:42,710
Accurate Assessment and Clear Growth.

75
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:45,730
Think about hospitals.

76
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:49,749
Almost all of them have CT
and MRI scans, but patients

77
00:04:49,815 --> 00:04:53,450
only trust a select few as
true diagnostic specialists.

78
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:57,467
That's the kind of authority JEI
should have: a learning program

79
00:04:57,523 --> 00:05:00,700
recognized for precise diagnosis
and real student growth.

80
00:05:02,450 --> 00:05:04,870
We also conducted a 3C analysis.

81
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:09,170
Our findings show that parents expect
more than basic English learning.

82
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:12,585
They want stronger literacy
skills, learning that matches

83
00:05:12,637 --> 00:05:15,550
each student's level, and
clear evidence of improvement.

84
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:19,370
They also want their children to gain
confidence through learning success.

85
00:05:21,020 --> 00:05:24,790
When we look at competitors, each has
already developed its own strengths.

86
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:28,210
Kumon focuses on repeated
practice and self-learning.

87
00:05:28,660 --> 00:05:31,150
Eye Level provides
literacy learning across

88
00:05:31,208 --> 00:05:33,640
