assessment-based self-learning.

94
00:05:53,390 --> 00:05:57,610
However, these strengths and learning results
are not yet clearly shown to parents.

95
00:05:59,260 --> 00:06:01,890
Therefore, we want to
maintain JEI's strengths

96
00:06:01,947 --> 00:06:04,120
in small-step and structured learning.

97
00:06:04,570 --> 00:06:07,918
At the same time, we plan to
strengthen literacy education and

98
00:06:07,972 --> 00:06:11,320
use precise assessment to provide
personalized learning paths.

99
00:06:11,770 --> 00:06:15,490
We also want to make each student's
progress and results easier to see.

100
00:06:15,940 --> 00:06:18,710
This will help us build a
stronger position in the market.

101
00:06:20,460 --> 00:06:24,970
We reviewed the main approaches and strengths
of major literacy programs in the U.S.

102
00:06:25,420 --> 00:06:29,350
Amplify builds background knowledge
to support reading comprehension.

103
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:33,630
Lexia uses learning data to identify
skills that need improvement.

104
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:37,410
i-Ready connects assessment results
with personalized learning.

105
00:06:37,860 --> 00:06:41,130
IXL tracks progress
across individual skills.

106
00:06:42,780 --> 00:06:45,650
We want to learn from these
programs and their strengths.

107
00:06:46,100 --> 00:06:50,580
However, our goal is not to make
literacy itself our only key difference.

108
00:06:51,030 --> 00:06:54,135
Instead, we want to combine
literacy learning with precise

109
00:06:54,189 --> 00:06:57,240
assessment, personalized
learning, and progress tracking.

110
00:06:57,690 --> 00:07:01,280
Through this approach, we aim to offer
a different learning experience.

111
00:07:02,930 --> 00:07:07,500
Our English team is continuing to study
major U.S. literacy programs in more detail.

112
00:07:07,950 --> 00:07:10,825
Based on this research, we are
working to define the unique

113
00:07:10,874 --> 00:07:14,090
